{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed581286445/13/codegen_prompts/6.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/13`\n- 题号：`6`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed581286445/13/6.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"6\">\n从多米诺骨牌信号塔沿排列方向发射颜色射线，射线在遇到 2x2 棱镜方块时发生 90 度偏转并变为棱镜的第二种颜色后继续传播。\n\nInput structure：\n- 背景为最常见颜色。\n- 网格中有若干个\"信号塔\"：每个信号塔是一个两像素的同色多米诺骨牌（水平排列或垂直排列）。\n- 网格中还有若干个\"棱镜\"对象：每个棱镜是一个 2x2 的实心正方形，由两种颜色构成——其中一条对角线上的两个像素为一种颜色（棱镜入射色），另一条对角线上的两个像素为另一种颜色（棱镜出射色）。\n- 信号塔和棱镜之间不接触，互相不重叠。\n\nRule：\n- 从每个水平多米诺的左端向左和右端向右各发射一条射线；从每个垂直多米诺的上端向上和下端向下各发射一条射线。射线颜色为信号塔的颜色。\n- 射线沿行或列逐像素前进，将经过的背景像素染为射线当前颜色。\n- 当射线到达某个棱镜 2x2 方块的边缘时，射线停止，不染棱镜像素。然后从棱镜的与射线入射方向垂直的一侧（顺时针旋转 90 度的方向）发出一条新射线，新射线颜色为棱镜的出射色。\n- 新射线继续沿直线传播，直到遇到网格边界、另一个棱镜、或另一个信号塔为止。\n- 若两条射线经过同一像素，后处理的射线覆盖先处理的（按信号塔从左到右、从上到下的顺序处理）。\n- 信号塔和棱镜的原始像素保持不变。\n\nKey insight：\n多米诺骨牌的方向编码了射线的发射轴线，2x2 棱镜同时编码了\"在哪里转弯\"和\"转弯后变成什么颜色\"。解题者需要先发现射线的传播方向由多米诺朝向决定，再发现棱镜的偏转与变色双重功能，两层机制叠加才能推导完整输出。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/f0f8a26d, train/11dc524f, train/6165ea8f, train/ad173014, train/3bd292e8, train/d93c6891, train/bd5af378, train/14b8e18c\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"f0f8a26d\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4357\nmechanism=0.4955\nlexical=0.0138\ncode_feature=0.8000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, code:rotation, object:line_segment, object:sprite, operation:draw_line, operation:reflect, operation:rotate, operation:sort_order, output:same_size, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/f0f8a26d.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/f0f8a26d.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRotate every foreground bar 90 degrees around its own center on the same canvas.\n\nInput structure\nThe background is the dominant color, and all foreground pixels share one color.\nEach 4-connected foreground object is a solid one-cell-thick horizontal or vertical\nbar with odd length, with single-pixel bars allowed.\n\nRule\nClear the canvas to the background, then redraw every bar with its midpoint, length,\nand color preserved while swapping horizontal and vertical orientation.\n\nKey insight\nThe bars are independent objects: their centers and lengths identify the output\nplacement, so no matching, ordering, or global symmetry is needed.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"4-connected monochromatic foreground bars on a dominant background\",\n  \"transform\": \"rotate each odd-length horizontal or vertical bar 90 degrees about its midpoint; preserve its color and length, with single-pixel bars unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"11dc524f\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3826\nmechanism=0.4174\nlexical=0.0137\ncode_feature=0.8000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, code:rotation, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, object:square, operation:draw_line, operation:reflect, relation:adjacent, relation:overlap\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/11dc524f.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/11dc524f.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide the non-square sprite to the square anchor and replace the anchor with the sprite's mirror image.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the most common color.\n- There is one 8-connected non-background sprite that is not a solid 2x2 square.\n- There is one solid 2x2 square anchor in another non-background color.\n\nRule:\n- Move the sprite straight toward the anchor along their unique cardinal separation until it touches the anchor's near edge.\n- Reflect the moved sprite across that near edge and draw the reflected copy in the anchor color.\n- Clear the original locations; the output keeps only the moved sprite and reflected anchor-color copy.\n\nKey insight:\n- The 2x2 square marks the mirror line: its side facing the sprite becomes the contact edge for a two-color reflected pair.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"8-connected non-square foreground sprite s\",\n  \"dst\": \"solid 2x2 square anchor d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s faces d by cardinal separation with overlapping span\",\n  \"transform\": \"translate s to touch d's facing edge, mirror s across that edge in d.color, and clear originals\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"6165ea8f\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4009\nmechanism=0.4681\nlexical=0.0128\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, code:rotation, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, object:square, operation:draw_line, operation:reflect, operation:rotate, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6165ea8f.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/6165ea8f.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nBuild a color-labeled shape-equivalence table from the objects listed on the right edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background contains one main 4-connected object for each foreground color.\n- The rightmost column has one singleton pixel of each foreground color, listed top-to-bottom.\n- Those singleton pixels define the row and column order of the output table.\n\nRule:\n- Normalize each main object to its tight mask and compare masks up to rotation or reflection.\n- Draw 2x2 color labels across the top and down the left, separated by one background row/column.\n- For each off-diagonal table cell, paint a 2x2 red block when the two labeled objects have the same shape under rotation/reflection, otherwise paint a 2x2 grey block.\n- Leave diagonal cells and all separators as background.\n\nKey insight:\n- Object positions and original orientations are distractors; the relation is dihedral shape equivalence, while the right-edge legend fixes the table order.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"main colored objects plus right-edge singleton color legend\",\n  \"dst\": \"2x2-labeled pairwise relation table in legend order\",\n  \"transform\": \"normalize each object's mask; red-fill off-diagonal table cells for object pairs with the same shape under rotation/flip, grey-fill all other off-diagonal cells; diagonal cells and separators remain background\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"square table with side length 3 * legend length + 2\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"ad173014\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3840\nmechanism=0.4202\nlexical=0.0113\ncode_feature=0.8000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, code:rotation, object:sprite, object:square, operation:draw_line, operation:recolor, operation:rotate, operation:sort_order, output:same_size, relation:adjacent\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/ad173014.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/ad173014.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRecolor each framed interior mask with the color from the next red frame clockwise around the blue connector cycle.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid contains hollow red square frames connected pairwise by blue line components.\n- The blue components connect the frames into one cycle, with every frame touching exactly two blue components.\n- Each frame interior contains background plus exactly one non-background color mask.\n\nRule\n- Sort the red frames clockwise by their centers around the cycle.\n- Keep each frame's interior mask shape in place, but recolor it with the interior color from the next clockwise frame.\n- Leave the red frames, blue connectors, background, and interior background holes unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The colored masks do not move; the blue cycle gives the order in which their colors rotate.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"the unique non-background interior color of each red frame, with frames ordered clockwise around the blue connector cycle\",\n  \"dst\": \"the interior foreground mask of each red frame in the same clockwise frame order\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"source color at clockwise rank k recolors destination mask at rank k-1, wrapping around the cycle\",\n  \"transform\": \"recolor each destination mask in place; keep mask shapes, frame borders, blue connectors, and background unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"3bd292e8\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3917\nmechanism=0.4550\nlexical=0.0114\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, code:rotation, object:line_segment, operation:draw_line, operation:recolor, operation:reflect, output:same_size, relation:adjacent, relation:between, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/3bd292e8.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/3bd292e8.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRecolor wall-separated background regions alternately, starting with grey in the lower-left region.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has one dominant background color and one foreground wall color.\n- The wall pixels form one or more 4-connected one-cell-thick segments.\n- Each wall segment separates exactly two 4-connected background regions.\nRule\n- Keep all wall pixels unchanged.\n- Label the 4-connected background regions and connect two labels when they\n  touch opposite sides of the same wall segment.\n- Color the region containing the lower-left corner grey, then flip between\n  grey and green across every wall adjacency.\nKey insight\n- The red walls define a bipartite map of regions; the lower-left background\n  region fixes which side of the alternating coloring is grey.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
